course: dictionary
lesson: 556
title: One small word, many meanings
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: The word «au» is tiny, but it does different jobs. It is not an English word on its own, so you need its context to know which meaning fits. Look at the words and sentences around it, and at where you found it.
explain: In French, «au» means «to the», «at the» or «in the» before a masculine word: «au parc» is «to the park» and «au revoir» is «goodbye». In a science book, «Au» is a chemical symbol for gold. On a website, «.au» is short for Australia.
explain: English borrows some phrases too: an «au pair» is a young person from abroad who lives with a family and helps look after the children. Always check your meaning by putting it into the sentence. If it still makes sense, you have found the right one.
fact: Context means the words and sentences around a word, and they show you which meaning of «au» is right.
fact: «Au» means «to the», «at the» or «in the» before a masculine word, as in «au parc» (to the park) and «au revoir» (goodbye).
fact: «Au» is the chemical symbol for gold, from the Latin word «aurum».
fact: «AU» is short for Australia, and in space science it is an astronomical unit: about 150 million km, the distance from the Earth to the Sun.
fact: To an English ear, French «au» sounds like «oh».
exercise: «Je vais au parc.» What does au mean in this French sentence? | *To the | Because of the | Under the | With a
exercise: «The chemical symbol Au is on the periodic table.» What does Au stand for? | *Gold | Iron | Silver | Aluminium
exercise: «The website address ends in .au.» What does AU mean here? | Austria | A young helper who lives with a family | *Australia | Astronomy club
test: «1 AU is about 150 million km.» In a space book, what does AU mean? | A young helper who lives with a family | *An astronomical unit, the distance from the Earth to the Sun | Australia | Gold
test: «Au revoir, Maman!» What does au revoir mean? | Good morning | *Goodbye | Hello | Thank you
exam: Why must you use context to work out what «au» means? | Because au is always spelled the same way in every language and means gold | *Because au has several meanings: a French word, the symbol for gold, and a short form of Australia | Because au is a Latin word for the Sun | Because au is only a French word and never means anything else
